{"insertText":{"location":{"index":144577,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"text":"\nAll test videos were analyzed. Coverage was 100%, and no video ended in a preprocessing failure or an insufficient-evidence state, so no result depends on how failed videos would have been counted. The test sets differ in their dependence structure. Each FaceForensics++ test set contains 70 source clusters of four videos, and DeeperForensics-1.0 contains 201 real–fake source pairs. Celeb-DF v2 contains 978 videos, but all 843 of its fake videos lie in nine target-identity clusters, so its fake class rests on nine independent clusters and its intervals are approximate. Because the clusters are keyed by target identity, whether the identity of the swapped-in source face was also held out could not be verified from the archived records."}},
