{"updateTextStyle":{"range":{"startIndex":145296,"endIndex":145297,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":12,"unit":"PT"}},"fields":"bold,italic,underline,backgroundColor,fontSize"}},
{"insertText":{"location":{"index":144577,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"text":"\nRQ1 asked: To what extent does SwinFusion++ improve video-level deepfake detection performance compared with standalone Swin Transformer and standalone Video Swin Transformer under in-distribution and cross-dataset evaluation, in terms of Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1-Score, and ROC-AUC? The principal evidence is the fixed-recipe comparison, in which Swin-B, Video Swin-B, and SwinFusion++ were trained with the identical recipe, so a difference between them is not due to unequal tuning. The BO-selected SwinFusion++ is reported afterward as a configured system with unequal optimization effort."}},
